    "text": "MotionForesight predicts future 3D trajectories for points on a manipulated object given a short observed video context of human-object interaction.",
    "topic": "MotionForesight prediction"
  },
  {
    "text": "MotionForesight is trained using only the observed frames from complete clips, replacing future RGB and geometry with learned mask latents.",
    "topic": "Training methodology"
  },
  {
    "text": "MotionForesight outperforms substantially larger models that use over a million training videos, demonstrating efficient repurposing of video priors into explicit geometric forecasts for embodied intelligence.",
    "topic": "Performance comparison"
  },
  {
    "text": "The approach redirects priors from pixel prediction models toward future 3D scene flow by using a dense 3D tracker built on a pretrained video model.",
    "topic": "Model architecture"
  },
  {
    "text": "MotionForesight uses a short observed video context to predict future 3D trajectories, indicating reliance on memory of recent visual input.",
    "topic": "Memory usage"
